    {
      "text": "Beware of pushing strongly on its squishy body, as it makes a mysterious purple fluid ooze out.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its shape and coloration vary, depending on its habitat.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beware of pushing strongly on its squishy body, as it makes a mysterious purple fluid ooze out.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its shape and coloration vary, depending on its habitat.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "For the most part, it makes its home along the seashore. Its color and form differ according to its habitat and the quality of its food.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Purple mucus sticks to the hands of anyone who touches it. Take care, as the substance is troublesome to wash off.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "While they normally live in the sea, they can function on land, too, until their skin dries out.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it senses danger, a purple liquid oozes out of it. The liquid is thought to be something like greasy sweat.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon’s habitat shapes its physique. According to some theories, life in warm ocean waters causes this variation to develop.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Subjecting this Pokémon to a strong force causes it to secrete a strange purple fluid. Though harmless, the fluid is awfully sticky.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Found in abundance on seashores bordering warm waters. Shellos are unexpectedly friendly and will crawl toward any person they see. Take care not to get coated in mucus!",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
